      {
        "Id": "a9c5205ed6694b4c9bcd3c0a3f2827fa",
        "Title": "HOW TO USE  -  link the CAD with the stair, select it in Revit, Run\nThe stair is found by its SHAPE on any layer: 6+ parallel tread lines, evenly spaced (straight, L, U / dog-leg). Concrete + landings + handrails.\nRiser = floor-to-floor height / number of risers (never above Max riser). Top level L3 = same stair L1->L2 and L2->L3.\nRe-run = stairs from this CAD are rebuilt (not doubled). Wrong way up? switch Flip direction.",
        "DescriptionText": null,
        "IsExpanded": true,
        "WidthAdjustment": 0.0,
        "HeightAdjustment": 0.0,
